Report read errors in sort.
A read error ends the line reader's input just as end of file does, and
sort never checked the stream's error flag, so it sorted and wrote
whatever had been read and exited 0. Check the result of
fclose_if_not_stdin(), which reports the error flag, and die with the
file name, as sort already does when a file cannot be opened.

---
 coreutils/sort.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/sort.c
+++ b/coreutils/sort.c
@@ -632,7 +632,8 @@
 			lines = xrealloc_vector(lines, 6, linecount);
 			lines[linecount++] = line;
 		}
-		fclose_if_not_stdin(fp);
+		if (fclose_if_not_stdin(fp))
+			bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die(*argv);
 	} while (*++argv);
 
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_SORT_BIG
